# Cloudflare Pages headers file. Has no effect locally — Pages applies it at the
# edge. Syntax: a path pattern on its own line, then indented "Name: value" lines.
#
# ⚠️ STRUCTURE: the CSP is deliberately NOT on /* any more. Two pages carry two
# different policies (the front door signs in, /todo must never gain JS), and a
# path that matched two CSP rules could end up with two CSP headers — which
# browsers enforce as the INTERSECTION, silently breaking sign-in. So /* carries
# only the non-CSP safety headers, and each page's CSP lives on its own exact
# rules. A NEW page added under public/ therefore ships with NO CSP until a rule
# is added here — add one, strict by default, in the same commit as the page.
#
# ⚠️ TRAILING SLASH, discovered 2026-08-14 building /status: Pages 308s a
# subdirectory request from its bare form ("/admin") to the trailing-slash
# form ("/admin/") before serving the file, and a _headers path pattern
# matches ONLY the exact request path — "/admin" does NOT also match
# "/admin/". The 308 itself carries the CSP (it matched), but the redirect's
# empty body is never rendered, so the browser applies whatever headers
# arrive on the FINAL 200 — which had none. Net effect: /admin and /todo have
# been serving their real page with **no CSP at all** since each was added;
# only curling the bare path (which the deploy checklists happen to do)
# looked like proof it worked. Fixed here by adding an explicit
# trailing-slash duplicate of every subdirectory rule; a future page under
# public/<name>/ needs both "/<name>" and "/<name>/" for this reason.
#
# THE FRONT DOOR + /admin POLICY (estate-auth-design.md §7.2 — the old
# "zero external requests" rule was overturned WITH the reasoning on record;
# the in-file comment atop index.html carries it). Allow-listed, not open:
#   script-src  'self' + www.gstatic.com (Firebase SDK modules, the same CDN
#               builds every audiobook page ships) + apis.google.com (the
#               sign-in popup's helper — Google-controlled, needed by some
#               popup flows; remove if observed unused).
#   connect-src the two estate Workers (index = search, auth = the /admin
#               API whose CORS names exactly https://heygabi.ai) + Firebase
#               auth endpoints (identitytoolkit = sign-in, securetoken =
#               token refresh). /admin ONLY additionally names the two app
#               Workers (library, boardgames) — the federated role columns
#               read/write each app's own /api/admin surface, whose CORS is
#               locked to this origin; the front door has no business there,
#               so its rule does not carry them.
#   frame-src   the Firebase auth iframe on the project's authDomain, and
#               accounts.google.com for the sign-in flow.
#   img-src     'self' data: (the inline SVG favicon) + the estate's cover
#               hosts + EVERY host the real pushed index rows hotlink,
#               MEASURED 2026-08-14 from the 2,259 production rows (the
#               as-you-type search renders cover thumbnails, so a missing
#               host silently blanks a thumbnail): covers.heygabi.ai
#               (1,077 audiobook), bookcovers.heygabi.ai + library.heygabi.ai
#               (library), cf.geekdo-images.com (196 games) and the games'
#               long third-party tail (shopify/gamefound/dndbeyond/
#               dicethrone/cloudfront/squarespace/kickstarter/itch/
#               loottavern/d20/backerkit/bigcommerce — each appears in real
#               rows; no https: wildcard on purpose). That tail is the
#               rehost-to-R2 case (improvement-proposals §3): when covers
#               move to estate hosts, prune this list back. Plus Google
#               avatars. A cover on any other host renders a clean blank
#               box (find.js keeps the slot, drops the broken image).
#   style-src   'self' (assets/estate-theme.css — the theme system) +
#               'unsafe-inline' for the per-page <style> blocks; with inline
#               SCRIPT still blocked there is no injection vector to
#               leverage a nonce against (unchanged reasoning).
#   font-src    'self' ONLY — every theme font (Rajdhani, Share Tech Mono,
#               Bangers, Luckiest Guy) is a committed woff2 under
#               assets/fonts/, the same no-third-party reasoning the games
#               repo used when it committed its own. Google Fonts hosts stay
#               OFF this list on purpose.
# Still absolutely absent: analytics, third-party font requests, CDN frameworks.
#
# /todo KEEPS THE ORIGINAL default-src 'none' NO-JS POLICY. Its filter is
# CSS-only radios and its README says it must never acquire JavaScript; the
# strict CSP is the enforcement of that sentence.
#
# /status (added 2026-08-14, the estate status page — "I want to see all the
# pipelines"). No sign-in, so no Firebase SDK and no script-src beyond
# 'self'. connect-src names exactly the five hosts status.js fetches: the
# four /api/health origins it reads as JSON (index/auth/library/games) plus
# the audiobook site root, whose /dev/ lane is checked at the same origin so
# it needs no separate entry. No img-src beyond the inline SVG favicon —
# this page renders no covers. frame-src, form-action and base-uri all stay
# 'none' — nothing on this page ever needs them.
#
# /universes (added 2026-08-15, one row per estate universe expanding to
# /api/universe/:name). Signs in (universes.js reuses estate-auth.js), so it
# carries the front door's script-src (Firebase SDK) and frame-src (the
# popup/redirect sign-in flow), but connect-src drops auth.heygabi.ai — this
# page shows no admin surface and never calls that Worker. img-src is the
# SAME cover-host allow-list as the front door's own "/" rule below, copied
# verbatim rather than hand-maintained separately, because a universe's rows
# can carry a cover from any source the estate indexes (audiobook, library or
# game) — read that list fresh before editing either one; a copy that drifts
# from "/" is how a cover host silently blanks here but not there.

/status
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; connect-src https://index.heygabi.ai https://auth.heygabi.ai https://library.heygabi.ai https://boardgames.heygabi.ai https://audiobooks.heygabi.ai; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

